Package: skipMCA
Type: Package
Title: Questionnaire Skips in Multiple Correspondence Analysis Indices
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("A. F. M. Tahsin", "Shahriar", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "tshahriar@isrt.ac.bd",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0003-0565-0803")))
Description: Audits how much of a questionnaire filter each coding of skipped
    items carries into an index built by multiple correspondence analysis
    (MCA). Items asked only of respondents who pass one filter question can
    dominate the first MCA axis, which then follows the filter. The package
    computes the closed-form squared correlation ratio between eligibility and
    each coded item, an inertia ratio comparing the filtered items with the
    other items, the share of the index explained by eligibility, and a budget
    check, all from development data. It fits MCA indices under missing single
    (the skip as its own category), the skip as the reference answer, subset
    (specific) MCA, or missing fuzzy average (van der Heijden and Escofier
    2003), places new respondents by the transition formula, and scores
    allocations against a known need criterion.
